<title>UK: Pharmacia says Edronax wins UK approval.</title>
<headline>Pharmacia says Edronax wins UK approval.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish-U.S. drugs group Pharmacia &amp; Upjohn Inc said on Thursday that the British Medicines Control Agency had granted marketing approval for Edronax tablets for treatment of depressive illness.</p>
<p>In a statement the company said the UK would be used as the reference state for approval throughout the European Union.</p>
<p>&quot;Edronax will be an important new treatment option in a therapeutic area characterized by a high unmet medical need of depressed patients,&quot; said Goran Ando, executive vice-president for worldwide science and technology.</p>
</text>
